.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-591-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-592-# Tag — annotated + GPG-signed INLINE. The tag message is the Owner-visible
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-593-# artifact; pushing it starts release.yml AND npm-publish.yml.
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-594-#
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-595-# Two fail-closed guards run first, for RC and stable ALIKE. Scoping them to
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-596-# `--stable` would let an rc.N ship a post-review commit and then become the
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-597-# unreviewed baseline the GA is promoted from.
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-598-#
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-599-# THE LOCAL ASSERT IS NOT ENOUGH — say it out loud. A tag signed by hand skips
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-600-# this driver entirely, and the pair-rail step 15 recomputes inputs_hash only
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-601-# over `pair-rail-inputs-hash-manifest.txt`, which deliberately EXCLUDES the
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-602-# bump surfaces (including them would make every legitimate bump change the
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-603-# inputs_hash and break the verdict replay). The same restricted-delta assert
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-604-# therefore goes SERVER-SIDE into `.github/workflows/release.yml` in PLAN-166
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-605-# W1. release.yml is canonical: it changes under the GPG ceremony, not here.
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh:606:# `_release_tag_guard.py` is the reference implementation for both.
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-607-# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/scripts/local/release.sh-608-tag() {
