.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-1-#!/usr/bin/env python3
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-2-# ============================================================================
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py:3:# _release_tag_guard.py — the two fail-closed asserts `tag()` runs before it
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-4-# asks the Owner's key to sign anything.
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-5-#
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-6-# WHY THIS EXISTS (v1.3.0-rc.1 re-pass, F2 + the F1/F2 composite risk):
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-7-#
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-8-#   (a) ANCESTRY. Nothing verified that the commit being tagged is on main.
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-9-#       `bump` could create a local commit AFTER the preflight proved CI green
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-10-#       for a different SHA, and `tag()` would sign that never-tested tree.
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-11-#       Two DISTINCT failures, never merged into one message: "could not talk
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-12-#       to origin" (network/offline — has a named escape hatch) and "HEAD is
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-13-#       not an ancestor of origin/main" (a real governance stop). The fetch and
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-14-#       the merge-base are SEPARATE statements: a failed fetch followed by a
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-15-#       merge-base against a stale ref is a FALSE APPROVAL.
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-16-#
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-17-#   (b) RESTRICTED DELTA. The invariant is "nothing landed after what the
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-18-#       re-pass reviewed, other than the verdict itself". The anchor is the
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-19-#       REVIEWED PARENT recorded in the signed verdict — one rule for RC and
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-20-#       GA. Anchoring on "the last RC" is wrong in both directions: for the GA
.claude/scripts/local/_release_tag_guard.py-21-#       it coincides by accident, and for an rc.2 it would reject the very
